                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "31da2426-60bf-3430-857b-f0b91772147a",
                        "entry_id": "15824b4a-6a79-34bc-b01f-fe1cc453365b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The firn or snowfield at the head of a glacier."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04d52f3f-c2af-4ff5-8ec1-da635ccf1074",
                                "sense_id": "31da2426-60bf-3430-857b-f0b91772147a",
                                "text": "Then we started up a rise, and to our annoyance found ourselves amongst crevasses once more—very hard, smooth névé between high ridges at the edge of crevasses, and therefore very difficult to get foothold to pull the sledges."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "68c09197-0077-3db0-b5fa-92eb693fcaaa",
                        "entry_id": "15824b4a-6a79-34bc-b01f-fe1cc453365b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Young, granular snow on a glacier, which has been partially melted and refrozen since deposition, but has not yet turned into firn by surviving a full season of ablation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d4eb60d3-ab09-4014-8cdd-8d80853fc96f",
                                "sense_id": "68c09197-0077-3db0-b5fa-92eb693fcaaa",
                                "text": "Haast's 1864 paper does not explain exactly why the glaciers should have come and gone as they did, but it appears that he believed that the onset of glaciation was due to the formation of his \"high, plateau-like\" range of mountains, acting as a moisture trap, with consequent névé accumulation on a grand scale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "65815e1e-8814-4e09-b525-68a7b2ee89af",
                                "sense_id": "68c09197-0077-3db0-b5fa-92eb693fcaaa",
                                "text": "The rate of snow-névé accumulation may change many times during the glacier lifetime due to changes in climatic conditions or other factors. Calculations show that the glacier responds fairly quickly to such changes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
